WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.010
- Hi, it's Rie.

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:03.070
Today, a friend will be challenging me

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:06.510
to take a popular food and Make it Fancy.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:09.130
Today's guest is Curly.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:09.963
- What's up, Rie?

00:00:09.963 --> 00:00:11.910
It is I, possibly one
of your favorite people.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.023
I don't know how you
can reinvent the wheel

00:00:14.023 --> 00:00:17.823
with Takis and make something
that's so good better,

00:00:17.823 --> 00:00:21.010
but if I know anything is for certain,

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.730
I know that the sun will come up tomorrow

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.170
and I know that Rie will
continue to kill it.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.303
So I'm so excited to see
what you come up with.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.240
- Takis.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.560
I have had Takis before.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.030
A lot of people said don't eat too much

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.950
'cause you get acid reflux.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.580
The lime is the key component.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.235
It's very addictive.

00:00:41.235 --> 00:00:43.135
(package rustling)

00:00:43.135 --> 00:00:44.710
(Rie crunching)

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.120
Oh, yeah.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.790
Takis spiciness comes right at you.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.710
It's spicy but it kind of disappears,

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.200
so you kind of want to keep eating.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.240
I like the flavor so I kinda want

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.880
to keep this flavor combination

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.410
'cause spicy and limey is very delicious,

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:04.400
and color is very bright red.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.310
So I think it's gonna be interesting

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:08.390
if we can use this red color.

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:12.420
I want to make this a meal
more than just a snack.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.990
My fingers are red.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.660
I forgot to bring my lipstick

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.840
so maybe I can just put on my lips.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.217
As always, I'm excited to Make it Fancy.

00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:23.410
(upbeat music)

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.180
All right, here's what I got.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.570
Limes, red onion, masa, microgreens.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:31.703
Shrimp, cilantro, orange, avocado.

00:01:31.703 --> 00:01:33.260
There's one more lime.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:36.870
Lemon, sparkling water, crema, and garlic.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.820
From the pantry I got vegetable oil,

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:43.080
sugar, flour, white vinegar, simple syrup,

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.140
salt, baking powder,
and dragon fruit powder.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.123
All right, let's get started.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.781
Make it Fancy.

00:01:51.781 --> 00:01:53.210
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.880
First step, one and a half cup water,

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.580
half cup sugar,

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.890
two teaspoon of salt,

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.650
four smashed garlic,

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.690
20 Takis.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:07.940
Bring this to a boil and steep
this for about 10 minutes.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.380
I think this is the great
thing for Halloween.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.230
It's like I'm poaching bones and blood.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.840
Maybe next year I'm gonna
just cook this in front

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:16.890
of my house.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.100
It has been simmering
for about 10 minutes.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.100
I'm going to strain over red onion.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.220
Let it pickle at least one hour.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.500
Cut avocado.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.850
The pit, I think I saw
Alex's Instagram story.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:31.280
You kinda hold and push.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.130
Perfect.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:36.380
I think I heard a lot of
people get injured hacking

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.530
and twisting.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:40.987
I think this TikTok hack is very useful.

00:02:40.987 --> 00:02:42.700
Add in a blender.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.320
Quarter cup of crema,

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.660
one tablespoon of lemon juice,

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:47.810
one garlic,

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.610
quarter cup of cilantro,

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:53.350
a little bit water first so
it's gonna blend smoothly.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:56.030
I'm going to blend until vibrant green.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.730
You know what Japanese
people call avocado?

00:02:58.730 --> 00:02:59.800
Morino bataa.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:02.100
It is butter from forest.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.860
All right, crema looks great.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.930
Add in a bowl and we are
moving on to next step.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:10.881
Two cups of Takis in a food processor.

00:03:10.881 --> 00:03:13.680
Put this in a bowl.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.950
I'm adding two tablespoon of ground Takis,

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.770
half cup of masa harina,

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:25.580
one tablespoon of dragon fruit
powder just for the color.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.550
Quarter teaspoon of salt.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:28.740
Mix it up.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.600
Oh, this is beautiful.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.790
Add quarter cup of warm water to start

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.370
and I'm going to keep adding as needed.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:40.125
- [Producer] When do you
think Takis were invented?

00:03:40.125 --> 00:03:40.958
- 1962.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.100
- [Producer] 1999.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:44.950
- Wow!

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:47.908
So it's a recent invention.

00:03:47.908 --> 00:03:50.367
- [Producer] Introduced
in America in 2006.

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:53.020
- I came to New York in 2007.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:56.500
So me and Taki were in
America very similar time.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.860
We are both immigrants.

00:03:57.860 --> 00:03:59.600
While dough is coming together,

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.970
so I'm going to use my hand.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.330
This is so pretty.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:06.410
The texture should be like Play-Doh.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.680
It's slightly wet but it's not sticky.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.910
We are going to cover this

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:13.040
and let it sit in room
temperature about one hour.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.970
But we have plenty things to do.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:17.210
Now it's a little bit firmer and I'm going

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:22.210
to divide into four and make
it like a golf size ball.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.464
Another torture device.

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:26.522
(producer laughing)

00:04:26.522 --> 00:04:29.030
Put parchment paper on the bottom.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:32.653
Another parchment paper and press it.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.640
Beautiful.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.910
I used tortilla press but if
you don't have it at home,

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.050
you can roll it up with rolling pin.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.710
Put this in the pan.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:44.970
Since this tortilla looks so pretty,

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.460
I will cook one minute per side.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.350
I don't want to make any
brown or brown color.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.070
- [Producer] Do you remember
the first time you met Curly?

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:56.060
- I just remember he is so
sweet and nice to everyone.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.290
I always wanted to be friend with him.

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.870
He brought his grandma for a Tasty shoot.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:04.110
He was holding her hand and one

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:08.320
of my coworker had a
fake cockroach on a desk.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.880
I think it was close to
Halloween or something.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:13.210
Curly just like quietly hide it

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.620
'cause he didn't want to scare her.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:16.900
I thought it was so cute.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:20.510
Okay, I see a little bubble
and I think it's ready.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.220
I want to keep this warm and
I don't want to break it,

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.660
so I'm going to put under the blanket.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.470
I always wanted to make this.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.920
My dream came true.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.630
I'm not using oil because
it's a non-stick pan.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:32.830
This looks cooked.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:35.270
Put this here, keep it warm.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.610
I'm going to finish making tortillas

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:38.780
and I'm going to move on.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.590
I'm heating up oil to 350.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:42.970
While oil is heating,

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:44.340
I'm going to make batter.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.800
One cup of flour,

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.390
quarter cup of Takis.

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:50.070
This is the powder I made earlier.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:52.140
Half teaspoon of baking soda,

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:54.080
half teaspoon of salt.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.240
Mix.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.330
When I make this dish I usually use beer,

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.030
but since Curly doesn't drink,

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:03.030
I'm using sparkling water.

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:04.880
You don't want to over mix it.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.310
Just like lightly mix.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:10.370
I have eight shrimps peeled and deveined.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.640
Season shrimp with salt.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.070
Coat with flour.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.790
Dredge in butter.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:18.670
It kind of look like what's the medicine?

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:20.210
Pepto-Bismol.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:25.210
I'm going to fry and I don't
want to overcrowd my oil

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:29.270
so I'm going to fry maybe four at a time.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.492
Wow.

00:06:30.492 --> 00:06:32.490
It kind of look like a giant Cheetos too.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:36.400
The sparkling water kinda
gives nice airy texture.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.430
Shrimp cooks very quickly

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.890
so I'm just cooking about two minutes.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:43.540
When the oil bubbles start coming

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.680
and shrimp is floating on the surface,

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:47.600
it's ready.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:49.830
It's cute but if somebody
who is eating this

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:51.010
for the first time,

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.800
they couldn't guess this is shrimp.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.090
It's basically a tempura 'cause tempura,

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.030
you want to use seltzer water.

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:59.110
I think, yeah, the baking soda

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:01.740
also gives nice fluffy texture too.

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:05.410
All shrimp are fried but we
have some more things to do.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:07.918
Leftover Takis powder,

00:07:07.918 --> 00:07:10.140
add in flaky salt,

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:12.480
toss a little bit, glass.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:16.330
Using lime, we are making mocktail.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:21.330
Put the glass upside down
and kind of around the rim.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:24.110
Oh, it's so cute.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:25.310
So festive.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:28.590
I'm gonna add ice each glass.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:29.520
Donk.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.670
Ice in a shaker.

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:34.000
Two ounces of orange juice.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.450
One ounce lemon juice.

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:39.400
Three ounce of lime juice,

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:40.691
and shake it.

00:07:40.691 --> 00:07:42.380
(mocktail rattling)

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:43.590
Ooh, it's icy.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.510
If you are making margarita,

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:47.790
obviously you have to add tequila.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.880
You usually use triple sec,

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:52.510
but triple sec also has alcohol in it

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:54.600
so I used orange juice instead.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:57.410
I'm topping off with sparkling water

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.530
and use lime as a garnish.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:02.587
All right, drinks are
done and time to move on.

00:08:02.587 --> 00:08:04.280
Put tortilla on the plate.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:06.720
First I'm adding avocado crema,

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:09.900
spread it using spoon's back.

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:14.690
Add shrimp, pickled onion,
and some microgreens.

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:17.540
Now I have some crema in a squeeze bottle.

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:19.560
Top with cilantro.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.410
Since we have some leftover Takis salt,

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:27.660
going to sprinkle and we are done!

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:30.493
(uplifting music)

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:37.613
Shrimp Takis tacos, very fancy.

00:08:39.758 --> 00:08:43.580
- I don't know where you
may have used the Takis,

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.350
but I'm assuming it's in the tortilla.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:49.230
- Yes, I made a tortilla with Takis.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:52.740
Yeah, I also made a
margarita virgin mocktail.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.147
- I just went to a
restaurant and I was like,

00:08:54.147 --> 00:08:55.770
"Hi, could I get a mocktail?"

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:57.403
And they were like, "We're out of mock."

00:08:57.403 --> 00:09:00.610
And I was "No, um, it's, no, mocktail,"

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:02.720
and she had no idea what I was saying.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:03.553
Someone has to be like,

00:09:03.553 --> 00:09:04.817
"Virgin, make it a virgin."

00:09:04.817 --> 00:09:06.639
"Oh yes, that we do."

00:09:06.639 --> 00:09:08.639
Cheers, cheers.
- Cheers.

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:10.680
- Oh my God.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:12.440
This is truly one of the
best tacos I've ever had.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.303
- Oh my God.

00:09:13.303 --> 00:09:14.960
- This is so, I'm from LA.

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:15.864
Born and raised in Hollywood.

00:09:15.864 --> 00:09:18.880
I'm from LA, hands down it's
one of the best I've ever had.

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:20.110
- Yes!

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:20.943
Takis savory!

00:09:20.943 --> 00:09:23.210
- Wow, cheers.
- Cheers.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:24.295
- Rie?

00:09:24.295 --> 00:09:25.128
- Yes.

00:09:25.128 --> 00:09:25.961
- How are you this perfect?

00:09:25.961 --> 00:09:26.794
(Rie gasping)

00:09:26.794 --> 00:09:27.740
Do you think that I could make this?

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:29.180
- Of course, it's easy.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:30.651
- Our Lord and savior, Rie.

00:09:30.651 --> 00:09:31.484
(Rie giggling)

00:09:31.484 --> 00:09:32.701
- We have one last thing to do.

00:09:32.701 --> 00:09:33.534
- Mm hm.

00:09:33.534 --> 00:09:34.600
One, two, three.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:35.809
- [Both] Make it Fancy.

00:09:35.809 --> 00:09:38.092
(both howling)

00:09:38.092 --> 00:09:40.842
(cheerful music)

